t", "desc": "Bug 2080747 - In TransportLayerDtls search for the single best cipher rather than the full advertised range.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332837\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335163\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/transport/transportlayerdtls.cpp"], "git_node": "9883bd15d3d6dae5a0f4937e7b421244c45a89d3", "git_parents": ["b0d1637a4eb0cc9543154c234e7093ecc17af2a7"], "node": "727981d8583053266f10e3fcd5c8d17061612b76", "parents": ["5eabe41ef4b3d14921d6f99bf3a19a2fc0d5cdd5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792770439, "git_changesets": ["b0d1637a4eb0cc9543154c234e7093ecc17af2a7", "9883bd15d3d6dae5a0f4937e7b421244c45a89d3"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "1066": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082365 - Don't panic when a quad segment's device size does not fit in i32.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nThe nine-patch and tile paths panicked in Size2D::to_i32 when a segment's\ndevice size was NaN or out of i32 range. Skip such segments instead.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334471\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335279\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "ef3463ee5c137b3dacad8333d9c2488302e695e9", "git_parents": ["9883bd15d3d6dae5a0f4937e7b421244c45a89d3"], "node": "3fb00b73c4f9bc52f29f46735253056577909f7f", "parents": ["727981d8583053266f10e3fcd5c8d17061612b76"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792770490, "git_changesets": ["ef3463ee5c137b3dacad8333d9c2488302e695e9"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "1067": {"changesets": [{"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2026491: Raise the file descriptor ceiling on macOS from 4096 to 65536.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nNSPR emulates poll() with select() on macOS, so a socket whose descriptor number is at or above the FD_SETSIZE the emulation was built with cannot be polled. Firefox therefore kept the descriptor limit at 4096 and asserts in AttachSocket that no socket reaches that number. A process that leaks descriptors hits the assert after a few thousand, which is the top macOS crash.\n\nThe three numbers move together to 65536 so that the emulation, the assert and the limit agree: FD_SETSIZE for the in-tree NSPR, the Darwin value in AttachSocket, and the soft limit set at startup. macOS accepts the larger limit in setrlimit and caps the effective value at kern.maxfilesperproc. The emulation's three fd_sets grow from 512 bytes to 8 KB each. They live on the stack and are zeroed per poll.\n\nThe new test occupies every descriptor below 4500 and checks that a request still goes through the socket transport service.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327425\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335854\n", "files": ["config/external/nspr/pr/moz.build", "netwerk/base/nsSocketTransportService2.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_socket_above_fd_setsize.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp"], "git_node": "ef1affa68f5d81ec7d84c46e0ea04b33cfc02125", "git_parents": ["ef3463ee5c137b3dacad8333d9c2488302e695e9"], "node": "feca2c512f3697e62ecc0e018519b8fe44483244", "parents": ["3fb00b73c4f9bc52f29f46735253056577909f7f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1792770563, "git_changesets": ["ef1affa68f5d81ec7d84c46e0ea04b33cfc02125"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "1068": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andy Leiserson \u003caleiserson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056172 - Update wgpu to upstream 1ab57112 (2026-10-12)  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334351\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/moz.yaml", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/src/client.rs", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/src/command.rs", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/binding_model.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/command/bundle.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/command/ray_tracing.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/command/render.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/command/render_command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/device/queue.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/device/ray_tracing.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/device/resource.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/indirect_validation/dispatch.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/indirect_validation/draw.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/indirect_validation/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/resource.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/scratch.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/timestamp_normalization/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/examples/halmark/main.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/examples/ray-traced-triangle/main.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/device.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dynamic/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dynamic/device.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dynamic/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/gles/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/gles/device.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/gles/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/metal/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/metal/device.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/noop/buffer.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/noop/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/noop/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/vulkan/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/vulkan/device.rs"], "git_node": "85e04c5be1ce4452d1029883aa338a2beb875077", "git_parents": ["ef1affa68f5d81ec7d84c46e0ea04b33cfc02125"], "node": "e638f814022